1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:06,074
Open the mouse pancreatic islet image from the
course and set the image type to Fluorescence.

2
00:00:06,314 --> 00:00:11,593
The blue channel shows nuclei, and the red
channel contains the insulin marker.

3
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:25,027
In Positive Cell Detection, the two intensity
thresholds answer different questions. First,
which nuclei are detected? Then, which of the
detected cells are positive for the marker?

4
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:32,108
Open Brightness and Contrast. Use the Show
column to view one channel at a time.

5
00:00:32,348 --> 00:00:39,532
Hide Channel One to see the blue nuclei in
Channel Two. Compare bright and dim nuclei
across the field.

6
00:00:39,772 --> 00:00:46,231
Now show Channel One and hide Channel Two. The
red signal is the marker we will use for
scoring.

7
00:00:46,471 --> 00:00:58,020
Turn both channels back on when comparing
detections with the image. These check boxes
control the viewer display. Set the detection
and scoring channels explicitly in the tool.

8
00:00:59,193 --> 00:01:08,617
Draw a small rectangle that includes some
bright and dim signal, then select it. The
three runs in this video use exactly the same
rectangle.

9
00:01:08,857 --> 00:01:19,366
Open Positive Cell Detection. For Detection
channel, choose Channel Two. Use the lesson
settings and leave cell expansion at five
micrometers.

10
00:01:19,606 --> 00:01:30,095
Set Score compartment to Cytoplasm, Channel One
mean. Keep Make measurements and Single
threshold enabled, then set Threshold One Plus
to thirty-five.

11
00:01:31,277 --> 00:01:42,156
In the Intensity parameters section, set the
detection Threshold to fifteen and run. In this
rectangle, QuPath finds two hundred and ninety-
three cells.

12
00:01:42,396 --> 00:01:51,014
Raise just this Threshold to twenty-five and
run again on the same region. Now QuPath finds
two hundred and sixty-one cells.

13
00:01:51,254 --> 00:02:01,863
The white marks point to examples where the
higher cutoff removes outlines. Check whether
faint nuclei are real and whether the lower
cutoff is also picking up background.

14
00:02:03,027 --> 00:02:11,616
Keep the detection Threshold at twenty-five. In
the scoring section, change Threshold One Plus
from thirty-five to seventy.

15
00:02:11,856 --> 00:02:20,450
The same two hundred and sixty-one cells are
still detected. The positive count drops from
one hundred and seventy-four to eighty-eight.

16
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:29,259
Follow the white marks. In those examples, the
outlines stay in place and change from red for
positive to blue for negative.

17
00:02:30,443 --> 00:02:37,982
First review the outlines against the blue
nuclei. Then review the positive labels against
the red insulin signal.

18
00:02:38,222 --> 00:02:47,241
Record the settings, compartment, and both
counts. The report script divides the positive
count by the positive plus negative counts.

19
00:02:47,481 --> 00:02:55,660
In this example, raising the positivity
threshold alone changes the fraction from about
sixty-seven percent to thirty-four percent.
